id: pm-g2zz
title: "As an agent in a million-item workspace, pm context and pm next give me a correct working set in under a second and a bounded token budget, without me knowing how big the workspace is"
description: "Agent story for the scale-out initiative (per capability-epic agent-story convention, changelog-excluded). Defines the experience bar the pm-9rxu children must jointly clear."
type: Story
status: open
priority: 2
tags[3]: agent-story,changelog-exclude,scale
created_at: "2026-07-06T21:24:57.706Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-08T13:24:48.622Z"
author: maintainer-agent
estimated_minutes: 60
acceptance_criteria: "On the synthetic 1M-item workspace: a fresh agent session can bootstrap (context -> next -> get -> claim) with every response sub-second and under the documented token budget; truncated views always say how to page deeper; no command requires the agent to adjust flags for workspace size"
parent: pm-9rxu
risk: low
confidence: high
expected_result: "A fresh agent session on a million-item workspace bootstraps through context, next, get and claim with every response sub-second and within the documented token budget, never adjusting flags for size."
